@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Stock correctness implementation plan
+
+1. Add a reusable HTTP 409 stock-conflict exception and preserve it through cart and checkout controller boundaries.
+2. Update cart creation, duplicate additions, single updates, and multi updates to validate the final quantities against each product's default stock before saving; keep zero/removal operations allowed and make multi updates all-or-nothing.
+3. Refactor checkout inventory handling to use order-line SKU/product lookup, validate all lines before changing anything, decrement exactly the requested quantities, and make the persistence operation transactional.
+4. Add cancellation inventory restoration keyed by order-line SKU, guarded so it runs only on the first cancellation, and reject transitions from canceled to another status with 409.
+5. Fix product v2 mapping so zero stock forces `available=false` and `canBePurchased=false`, while merchant-unavailable products remain unavailable.
+6. Add focused regression tests where the existing test structure permits, then build the affected Maven modules and run the relevant test suites.
