+# Stock correctness research
+
+## Scope traced
+
+- Cart HTTP endpoints are implemented by `sm-shop/.../store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java` and delegate to `store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java`.
+- Both checkout endpoints are in `sm-shop/.../store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`, then use `store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` and `sm-core/.../business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java`.
+- Inventory is stored as `ProductAvailability.productQuantity`; the default product inventory is selected by `ProductInventoryServiceImpl` and is also the quantity exposed by the product mappers.
+- Order status changes flow through `OrderApi.updateOrderStatus` and `OrderFacadeImpl.updateOrderStatus`.
+- Product v2 output is assembled by `ReadableProductMapper`.
+
+## Causes found
+
+1. Checkout inventory decrement in `OrderServiceImpl.process` calls `productService.getById(orderProduct.getId())`. `OrderProduct.id` is the order-line primary key, not the product id, so the wrong product can be updated or no product can be found. The code also logs an inventory mismatch and continues instead of refusing checkout.
+2. Checkout has an earlier validation in `OrderFacadeImpl.processOrderModel`, but the decrement is separate and there is no single atomic check-and-update for all lines. A failure after one update can therefore leave partial inventory changes unless the operation is transactional.
+3. Cart creation/addition and single/multi modification are spread across `createCartItem`, `createCartItems`, `readableShoppingCart`, `modifyCart`, and `modifyCartMulti`. They check product availability/quantity inconsistently, do not validate the final combined quantity for duplicate additions, and mutate the loaded cart before all requested changes have been validated. The multi check has a precedence bug (`&&`/`||`) and can reject quantity zero removals.
+4. The cart code checks every availability row rather than the same default availability used as the product's stock quantity. This can make an otherwise valid product fail or validate against the wrong row.
+5. `OrderFacadeImpl.updateOrderStatus` returns for the same status but otherwise only changes status/history. It neither restores stock on the first transition to `CANCELED` nor rejects transitions away from an already canceled order.
+6. `ReadableProductMapper` sets `canBePurchased` only when quantity is positive, but does not explicitly set `available` false for zero stock. The merchant-controlled product availability flag must remain authoritative when stock is positive, while zero stock must force both output flags false.
+7. REST error handling currently has no explicit 409 conflict exception. Several API methods wrap all exceptions into `ServiceRuntimeException`, whose handler is fixed at HTTP 400; checkout's authenticated endpoint directly sends HTTP 503 for every exception. A stock-conflict exception must be preserved and mapped to HTTP 409.
+
+## Affected behavior
+
+- Anonymous and authenticated checkout can decrement the wrong inventory and can create an order when stock is insufficient.
+- Adding a product, adding a duplicate product, single quantity changes, and multi changes can exceed stock or partially apply a request.
+- Removing/lowering a cart line can be blocked when the current product has become out of stock.
+- Canceling an order does not restore inventory; repeated cancellation and transitions out of canceled need explicit rules.
+- Product v2 availability/purchase flags can disagree with zero stock.
+
+## Implementation direction
+
+- Introduce one stock-conflict exception and REST handler returning 409.
+- Centralize selection of the default availability/stock and final-cart validation in the cart facade; validate all changes before persisting and allow zero quantities for removals.
+- Make checkout validate every ordered SKU and quantity before persistence, decrement the matching product availability exactly once per line, and run the database work transactionally.
+- Make status transitions restore the matching product by order-line SKU only on the first transition to `CANCELED`, and reject any later non-canceled transition.
+- Derive v2 `available` and `canBePurchased` from merchant availability plus positive stock.
